nt-type": "mp4", "height": 420}], "blurhash": "U14B:-IT00~qIAt8x^ITMdt7%MIAtlf4Vrbd", "full_resolution": [420, 746]}, "title": "\ud83d\udea8SOMETHING BIG IS COMING\ud83d\udea8", "last_comment_created": 1792197460751, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 3, "score_up": 44, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2111083917579047010", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVf23YhO", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 53, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8889422, "raw_content": "", "author": "blue5707", "created": 1792176609270, "profile_picture": "89ixTA9k3HEV", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Quality", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/johndoyle/status/2111083917579047010?s=46", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Liberals actually think that if we confiscated Elon Musk\u2019s wealth and spent it on Somalians then they\u2019d be inventing flying cars too.", "last_comment_created": 1792178845554, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 1, "score_up": 53, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 73, "created": 1792156602000, "id": "2111083917579047010", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1050086940190670848/qDoB9Vzv_normal.jpg", "displayName": "John Doyle", "username": "JohnDoyle"}, "content": "Liberals actually think that if we confiscated Elon Musk\u2019s wealth and spent it on Somalians then they\u2019d be inventing flying cars too.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 9222}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVf24wPV", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 17, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8889995, "raw_content": "Hi, I had an idea dawn on me the other day after speaking with an old co-worker that I haven't seen in years. He was a great guy, family man, worked hard, never complained much. He went through the wringer during the sleepy joe years. His wife left him, lost his job, became a drug addict. He is thankfully sober now, and working again, plus found a new woman he seems to be happy with.  \n\nWe spoke for almost half an hour in the super market catching up. His ex wife developed TDS among other mental problems usually associated with the left. She won't let him see the kids, turned them against him, and etc... He spent tons of money on a lawyer and it didn't work out for him. So he went down a pretty bad spiral until he was able to get back on his feet.  \n\n\nThe main point of this post is to draw attention to the systemic abuse that women can impose on a man in this country. If they want to, they can ruin a guy to complete annihilation (he almost committed suicide) with the assistance of our own government. He now has to pay this lady ungodly amounts of money and can't even see his kids or raise them. I got to thinking, I'm going to research this topic a bit, and what I found is sickening. It wasn't always like this in America and the statistics in each state are mind boggling and devastating not only to the men it affects, but also their children.  \n\n\nNow before you automatically take the side of the woman and use the common trope of \"it's for the well being and support of children\" consider this: what happened before legal extortion of men was allowed? There are many scholars and legal professionals who in fact agree that it violates numerous Constitutional Amendments. The more successful you are, the more you pay. The whole system is predominately ran by females who obviously in most cases side with the \"victim gender\". The amount of tax dollars used to keep that system running from the courts all the way down to case managers is shocking. There is no set in stone amount that is recognized as the necessary amount.  \n\nNow, for the custody part, they allow the legal kidnapping of children. The state assumes in some respects the total authority over the matter. Taking away parental rights from one to give to the other when in many cases there is no neglect, abuse, etc... how can we as a society allow this system to keep operating when it has so many detrimental qualities? Now look at the demographics. Also, compare with welfare which usually the female still qualifies for while pillaging the mans bank account.   \n\nA scorned woman can ruin not only the man, but the family. This should be a bi-partisan issue. But, it won't be because dumocrats seem to enjoy the destruction of the nuclear family. Look on social media, women rejoice over leaving their man over TDS. Maybe, just maybe if the Republicans promise to do something about this it could enhance certain areas voter turn out. What do you think?  \n\nAddendum: If one were to also correlate the people in prison for non-payment since income cannot be imputed, it may also lower crime.\n", "author": "Fortuity", "created": 1792198746444, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Fortuity", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Controversial Post...", "last_comment_created": 1792204662765, "content": "<p>Hi, I had an idea dawn on me the other day after speaking with an old co-worker that I haven't seen in years. He was a great guy, family man, worked hard, never complained much. He went through the wringer during the sleepy joe years. His wife left him, lost his job, became a drug addict. He is thankfully sober now, and working again, plus found a new woman he seems to be happy with.</p>\n<p>We spoke for almost half an hour in the super market catching up. His ex wife developed TDS among other mental problems usually associated with the left. She won't let him see the kids, turned them against him, and etc... He spent tons of money on a lawyer and it didn't work out for him. So he went down a pretty bad spiral until he was able to get back on his feet.</p>\n<p>The main point of this post is to draw attention to the systemic abuse that women can impose on a man in this country. If they want to, they can ruin a guy to complete annihilation (he almost committed suicide) with the assistance of our own government. He now has to pay this lady ungodly amounts of money and can't even see his kids or raise them. I got to thinking, I'm going to research this topic a bit, and what I found is sickening. It wasn't always like this in America and the statistics in each state are mind boggling and devastating not only to the men it affects, but also their children.</p>\n<p>Now before you automatically take the side of the woman and use the common trope of &quot;it's for the well being and support of children&quot; consider this: what happened before legal extortion of men was allowed? There are many scholars and legal professionals who in fact agree that it violates numerous Constitutional Amendments. The more successful you are, the more you pay. The whole system is predominately ran by females who obviously in most cases side with the &quot;victim gender&quot;. The amount of tax dollars used to keep that system running from the courts all the way down to case managers is shocking. There is no set in stone amount that is recognized as the necessary amount.</p>\n<p>Now, for the custody part, they allow the legal kidnapping of children. The state assumes in some respects the total authority over the matter. Taking away parental rights from one to give to the other when in many cases there is no neglect, abuse, etc... how can we as a society allow this system to keep operating when it has so many detrimental qualities? Now look at the demographics. Also, compare with welfare which usually the female still qualifies for while pillaging the mans bank account.</p>\n<p>A scorned woman can ruin not only the man, but the family. This should be a bi-partisan issue. But, it won't be because dumocrats seem to enjoy the destruction of the nuclear family. Look on social media, women rejoice over leaving their man over TDS. Maybe, just maybe if the Republicans promise to do something about this it could enhance certain areas voter turn out. What do you think?</p>\n<p>Addendum: If one were to also correlate the people in prison for non-payment since income cannot be imputed, it may also lower crime.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 13, "score_up": 17, "is_edited": true, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVf24wPR", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 17, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "hat", "id": 8889991, "raw_content": "", "author": "3Always3Victorious3", "created": 1792198482994, "profile_picture": "qE06F